96508	{"artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","entry":{"id":"f5b177fdb13821796d4d253448f5fd5ac297ed042e4b03854c9609f4108c6b9b","targetHeadHash":"6e3232f7e7c60b340eb79c1868bf5e5f935095fcb6c37c59e05221ccbaffe001","actor":{"id":"agent:design-review-daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{"party":"daemon"}},"timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:17:16.188Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":1,"contentHash":"b35c09ff49e63cc9b019e030957777ab15029de593bdc5505c1f5580dce3a4e7"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"Design review macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6 attempt 1","data":{"kind":"design-chunk-review","reviewId":"macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6","project":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc","artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","subject":{"project":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc","artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","kind":"LLD","canonicalPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","documentPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","reviewer":"daemon","workflow":{"kind":"issue","rootArtifactId":"ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f","requiredReferences":[{"role":"originating_issue","artifactId":"ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f","path":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md"}],"availableReferences":[],"notApplicableRoles":["PLAN","TASKS","BUILD","CR","DEF","HLD","sibling_stories"]}},"reviewer":"daemon","applicableAttempt":1,"status":"incomplete","binding":{"sourceRevision":{"number":1,"contentHash":"b35c09ff49e63cc9b019e030957777ab15029de593bdc5505c1f5580dce3a4e7"},"reviewedContentIdentity":"84b35629e7b712583748489d95b40e3d49d267770e5380579dedf1b3f21faa94","documentDigest":"0da7a172c708654992cf04fb5556786527bb3e188ec3cc1c197aa9bd6242965e","workflowDigest":"205362792ee2c850ee5e8c3ed5938d86633a344ce17336ab5b03b2d734785a13","author":"controller"},"preservationDigest":"5706e70778070c06b907e19e98112c73735fd2424d2e06fc735ebda37d142e45","schemaVersion":1,"submitted":{"artifactPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","attempt":1},"attempts":[{"number":1,"status":"incomplete","preparationKind":"planning","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"ea74f0a8a614b285d1f31639102a482f44b2a710ba3f8ab744e72c6cb4565543","document":"0da7a172c708654992cf04fb5556786527bb3e188ec3cc1c197aa9bd6242965e"},"contentIdentity":"84b35629e7b712583748489d95b40e3d49d267770e5380579dedf1b3f21faa94","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794413184997-au8a2s\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-11T16:09:35.631Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-11T16:00:50.440Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"unknown\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 190090,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"5d5478c61a25ac8f\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794413184997-au8a2s\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"777a81c01593254ca65864d942cd51e05e47d8d36e2368c8285aaea562726c37\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Design the approved macOS installer and automatic existing-install migration fix from ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"lifecycle\": {\n      \"status\": \"draft\",\n      \"revision\": {\n        \"number\": 1,\n        \"contentHash\": \"b35c09ff49e63cc9b019e030957777ab15029de593bdc5505c1f5580dce3a4e7\",\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-11T16:09:35.938Z\",\n        \"by\": {\n          \"id\": \"insrc:system\",\n          \"kind\": \"system\",\n          \"properties\": {}\n        }\n      },\n      \"signoffs\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 1\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"technical\",\n      \"prose\": \"The macOS installer initializes a managed launchd installation. A normal update stages a compatible release while the existing daemon is still running, then migrates ownership under a recoverable transaction. A previously stopped daemon stays stopped unless the user requested start.\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Design the approved macOS installer and automatic existing-install migration fix from ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal-shared\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"stageManagedInstallation\",\n          \"signature\": \"stageManagedInstallation(installation: ManagedInstallation, revalidate: () => Promise<void>, legacyCutover?: boolean): Promise<void>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"installation\",\n              \"type\": \"ManagedInstallation\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Pins the per-user root, immutable release, runtime and enabled state.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"revalidate\",\n              \"type\": \"() => Promise<void>\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Rechecks ownership before mutation.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"legacyCutover\",\n              \"type\": \"boolean\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Selects staging for a verified predecessor.\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<void>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The staged descriptor and selector are owned by the installation.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ownership-conflict\",\n              \"condition\": \"Conflicting install, job, run files, or mutation.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Fresh install enters via the normal installer after building and verifying a pinned release in a separate root. Confirm a usable same-user GUI launch domain and quiescent state.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Under one reservation publish owned enabled state, register and verify the per-user supervisor, and start a verified child only if requested. Honor --no-start. Recover or unwind interrupted activation before another start.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"completeLegacyMigration\",\n          \"signature\": \"completeLegacyMigration(gate: InstallationMutationGate, update: UpdateReservation, pins: ManagedUpdatePins): Promise<DaemonUpdateOutcome>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"gate\",\n              \"type\": \"InstallationMutationGate\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Serializes launchd, selector and child lifecycle mutations.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"update\",\n              \"type\": \"UpdateReservation\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Carries the verified predecessor and desired running state.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"pins\",\n              \"type\": \"ManagedUpdatePins\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Carries compatible prior and candidate release identities.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<DaemonUpdateOutcome>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Committed cutover, verified rollback, or recoverable ownership conflict.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"ownership-conflict\",\n              \"condition\": \"A trusted predecessor, exact exit, or rollback cannot be verified.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"The migration-capable installer or updater runs before any legacy stop or shutdown RPC. Stage and qualify the candidate separately and verify the predecessor from daemon status, exact owned run files and peer incarnation, or an exact passive same-user LaunchAgent. Keep rollback executable and metadata available.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Request cooperative exit over the authenticated legacy socket with an independent Darwin exit observer. A watchdog refusal counts as an exit only if that exact incarnation exited. Reconcile only pinned files. Remove a verified passive job only after exit; publish the candidate only after readiness. Restore the prior running or stopped state on verified rollback.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"ManagedInstallation and UpdatePredecessor\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"One state root owns one enabled selector and at most one supervisor job. The job owns at most one daemon child. During migration the reservation owns one candidate pin and one predecessor pin, with a launch-job descriptor only for a LaunchAgent predecessor. A direct predecessor records verified runtime, entry, owned run-file identities, and a rollback launch description; stopped installations record absence. Prior and candidate binaries stay separately recoverable. Persist a discriminated predecessor record with backward-compatible decoding of existing managed and legacy-job journals.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts\",\n          \"src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Predecessor identity is ambiguous or changes\",\n          \"detection\": \"Compare canonical root, runtime and entry, socket peer incarnation, pinned run-file identities, and exact launchd registration when present. Revalidate under the reservation before mutation.\",\n          \"response\": \"Refuse cutover and leave the existing service and files intact. Surface the reason through the ordinary update result.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Existing service remains available when it has not been stopped.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Legacy daemon fails to exit\",\n          \"detection\": \"The exit observer times out or sees a replacement rather than verified exit of the pinned incarnation.\",\n          \"response\": \"Do not start a candidate. Preserve live or foreign publications. Reconcile only if ownership and exit can later be established.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Update reports an actionable failure.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Candidate registration, readiness, or publication fails\",\n          \"detection\": \"Exact job or supervisor identity does not match, child never reaches authenticated readiness, or outcome persistence fails.\",\n          \"response\": \"Use journaled recovery to stop only the candidate generation, remove its exact job, restore the old selector and release, and restore prior running state. Keep the reservation fenced if rollback cannot be verified.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"A verified rollback reports failure and restores prior service.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Legacy updater starts shutdown before staging the migration release\",\n          \"detection\": \"The caller or installed release lacks the migration-capable preflight route.\",\n          \"response\": \"Ship the migration preflight in the normal installer and updated clients. Test the exact older shipped entry points and provide the supported upgrade entry point when an old caller cannot carry migration. Never report migration success from the legacy acknowledgement.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The user can use the ordinary supported install or update operation without launchd administration.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Fresh installation with --no-start\",\n          \"expected\": \"Install the managed lifecycle with no daemon child. The first ordinary start uses the supervisor.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Existing installation was stopped or is already managed\",\n          \"expected\": \"Preserve stopped state unless start was requested. Already managed updates use the normal managed transaction.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Legacy shutdown exits early after broker denial\",\n          \"expected\": \"Require independent exact exit and reconcile only pinned run files before admitting a successor. Record the early exit distinctly from a successful drain.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Concurrent installer, update, restart or retry\",\n          \"expected\": \"Single reservation owns cutover. A duplicate or interrupted operation reconciles its existing transaction before a new one starts.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Only one verified daemon owns the state root, PID file and socket.\",\n          \"source\": \"c2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Rollback preserves user settings, repositories, release and prior running state.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Linux retains its existing lifecycle.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Check predecessor admission, persisted pins and recovery decisions.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Fresh, managed, stopped legacy, direct legacy and passive LaunchAgent classifications\",\n            \"Refusal for foreign job, mismatched socket, changed descriptor and concurrent owners\",\n            \"Compatibility and backward decoding of existing journals\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Exercise user entry points and verified cutover with isolated roots.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Installer startup and --no-start\",\n            \"Release staging before legacy shutdown\",\n            \"Update from shipped broker-dependent predecessor through the normal supported entry point\",\n            \"Interrupted bootstrap, candidate failure, exact exit, rollback and retry\",\n            \"Linux installer and lifecycle regression\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"smoke\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Verify actual launchd registrations and processes in the macOS GUI domain.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Fresh installer followed by ordinary restart and verified PID change\",\n            \"Existing direct and LaunchAgent installs with the broker returning errno 1\",\n            \"Recovery LaunchAgent descriptor and runtime flags\",\n            \"Restored running or stopped state and unchanged settings and data after failure\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"Disposable macOS home with unique labels and isolated state\",\n            \"Pinned legacy and candidate builds\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"Fresh installer followed by ordinary restart and verified PID change\",\n            \"Installer startup and --no-start\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"Update from shipped broker-dependent predecessor through the normal supported entry point\",\n            \"Existing direct and LaunchAgent installs with the broker returning errno 1\",\n            \"Recovery LaunchAgent descriptor and runtime flags\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"Interrupted bootstrap, candidate failure, exact exit, rollback and retry\",\n            \"Restored running or stopped state and unchanged settings and data after failure\",\n            \"Linux installer and lifecycle regression\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"testFramework\": \"Node.js test runner through tsx, shell installer integration fixtures, and real macOS launchd smoke tests in a disposable user state root.\"\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"The standard installer starts directly via daemon-ctl. The selector-gated supervisor and explicit LaunchAgent migration controller exist. See the installer and migration discovery bundle in s1.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"Ordinary install and supported update commands establish a verified managed installation and use the per-user supervisor for future lifecycle calls.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Stage a compatible candidate and capture the canonical predecessor release and ownership before changing any live job or installation selector.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Acquire the installation reservation and verify the supported predecessor shape. Record running state and exact job, runtime, and publication identities.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"For a running predecessor, request cooperative shutdown and verify exact exit. If an owned passive LaunchAgent exists, remove only its pinned registration after exit. Reconcile only owned files.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Register the candidate supervisor and start one candidate only when the operation requests it or the predecessor was running. Verify service readiness, then publish the terminal outcome and release the reservation.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"action\": \"On failure, resume the journal to restore the prior release, launch job and running or stopped state. Report any unresolved ownership with the installation fenced.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"Keep existing installer switches, lifecycle command and IPC payload shapes. Keep Linux behavior. For the first upgrade, use a migration-capable normal installer or updated client before invoking older restart or shutdown behavior. A legacy binary that cannot stage the migration cannot promise automatic cutover. Decode existing managed and legacy-job journals.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": false,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": false\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Integrate with existing lifecycle transactions\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Install or migrate through the existing entry points and shared state.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Fresh installation establishes the managed selector through an owned transaction. Existing updates resolve and pin the predecessor before using the shared update reservation and rollback.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Single controller for launchd state and ownership.\",\n          \"Users keep their existing install and update commands.\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Requires a safe predecessor-specific exit path and compatibility checks.\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Migrate at the next start\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Defer cutover until an ordinary start observes a stopped installation.\",\n        \"approach\": \"An update stages the release and start performs cutover after verifying that the legacy daemon has exited and no legacy job can relaunch it.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Simpler cutover for stopped systems.\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"A healthy live installation whose broker cannot stop it may never reach the required state through normal commands.\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Works for quiescent installs but fails the live automatic migration goal.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": [],\n    \"sequenceDefinition\": {\n      \"id\": \"macos-install-cutover\",\n      \"narrative\": \"The sequence shows when the candidate is staged, when a verified predecessor may exit, and where readiness or rollback settles the operation.\",\n      \"participants\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"user\",\n          \"label\": \"Installer or updater\",\n          \"description\": \"User-facing install and update entry point.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Lifecycle controller\",\n          \"description\": \"Pins releases and owns the mutation reservation.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"legacy\",\n          \"label\": \"Legacy daemon and launchd job\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing release and exact job when present.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"supervisor\",\n          \"label\": \"Managed supervisor\",\n          \"description\": \"Registers and owns the candidate child.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"daemon\",\n          \"label\": \"Candidate daemon\",\n          \"description\": \"Publishes authenticated readiness and serves the state root.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"messages\": [\n        {\n          \"from\": \"user\",\n          \"to\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Stage and qualify candidate\",\n          \"description\": \"Keep the prior release available for rollback.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"controller\",\n          \"to\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Reserve and pin installation\",\n          \"description\": \"Verify state root and record predecessor ownership and prior running state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"controller\",\n          \"to\": \"legacy\",\n          \"label\": \"Drain existing daemon if running\",\n          \"description\": \"Authenticate the legacy socket and observe the pinned incarnation exit independently of the broker.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"legacy\",\n          \"to\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Verify exit and registration\",\n          \"description\": \"Reconcile owned publications and remove the pinned passive LaunchAgent after verified exit.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"controller\",\n          \"to\": \"supervisor\",\n          \"label\": \"Register and verify managed job\",\n          \"description\": \"Bind the job to the candidate and the installation state root.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"supervisor\",\n          \"to\": \"daemon\",\n          \"label\": \"Start if requested or previously running\",\n          \"description\": \"An idle install remains stopped.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"daemon\",\n          \"to\": \"supervisor\",\n          \"label\": \"Report authenticated readiness\",\n          \"description\": \"Confirm the child identity and its run files.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"supervisor\",\n          \"to\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Report verified state\",\n          \"description\": \"Commit the verified outcome, or unwind the candidate and restore the prior state on failure.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"controller\",\n          \"to\": \"user\",\n          \"label\": \"Return durable install or update result\",\n          \"description\": \"Report success only after verified readiness or verified stopped state.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"companions\": [\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"diagram-mermaid\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Sequence diagram\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"scripts/daemon-ctl.sh\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/update-runner.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c9\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1 — Design the approved macOS installer and automatic existing-install migration fix from ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794413184997-au8a2s`\n**HLD effective hash:** `777a81c01593...`\n\nThe macOS installer initializes a managed launchd installation. A normal update stages a compatible release while the existing daemon is still running, then migrates ownership under a recoverable transaction. A previously stopped daemon stays stopped unless the user requested start.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Diagrams](#4-diagrams)\n5. [Error paths](#5-error-paths)\n6. [Test strategy](#6-test-strategy)\n7. [Migration](#7-migration)\n8. [Alternatives considered](#8-alternatives-considered)\n9. [References](#9-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal-shared\n\n### 2.1 `stageManagedInstallation`\n\n```typescript\nstageManagedInstallation(installation: ManagedInstallation, revalidate: () => Promise<void>, legacyCutover?: boolean): Promise<void>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `installation: ManagedInstallation` — Pins the per-user root, immutable release, runtime and enabled state.\n- `revalidate: () => Promise<void>` — Rechecks ownership before mutation.\n- `legacyCutover: boolean` _(optional)_ — Selects staging for a verified predecessor.\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<void>` — The staged descriptor and selector are owned by the installation.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `ownership-conflict` when Conflicting install, job, run files, or mutation.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Fresh install enters via the normal installer after building and verifying a pinned release in a separate root. Confirm a usable same-user GUI launch domain and quiescent state.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Under one reservation publish owned enabled state, register and verify the per-user supervisor, and start a verified child only if requested. Honor --no-start. Recover or unwind interrupted activation before another start.\n\n### 2.2 `completeLegacyMigration`\n\n```typescript\ncompleteLegacyMigration(gate: InstallationMutationGate, update: UpdateReservation, pins: ManagedUpdatePins): Promise<DaemonUpdateOutcome>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `gate: InstallationMutationGate` — Serializes launchd, selector and child lifecycle mutations.\n- `update: UpdateReservation` — Carries the verified predecessor and desired running state.\n- `pins: ManagedUpdatePins` — Carries compatible prior and candidate release identities.\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<DaemonUpdateOutcome>` — Committed cutover, verified rollback, or recoverable ownership conflict.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `ownership-conflict` when A trusted predecessor, exact exit, or rollback cannot be verified.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- The migration-capable installer or updater runs before any legacy stop or shutdown RPC. Stage and qualify the candidate separately and verify the predecessor from daemon status, exact owned run files and peer incarnation, or an exact passive same-user LaunchAgent. Keep rollback executable and metadata available.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Request cooperative exit over the authenticated legacy socket with an independent Darwin exit observer. A watchdog refusal counts as an exit only if that exact incarnation exited. Reconcile only pinned files. Remove a verified passive job only after exit; publish the candidate only after readiness. Restore the prior running or stopped state on verified rollback.\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `ManagedInstallation and UpdatePredecessor` — invariant-change\n\nOne state root owns one enabled selector and at most one supervisor job. The job owns at most one daemon child. During migration the reservation owns one candidate pin and one predecessor pin, with a launch-job descriptor only for a LaunchAgent predecessor. A direct predecessor records verified runtime, entry, owned run-file identities, and a rollback launch description; stopped installations record absence. Prior and candidate binaries stay separately recoverable. Persist a discriminated predecessor record with backward-compatible decoding of existing managed and legacy-job journals.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts`\n- `src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts`\n- `src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts`\n\n## 4. Diagrams\n\n- [Sequence diagram](docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html)\n\n## 5. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **Predecessor identity is ambiguous or changes** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: Compare canonical root, runtime and entry, socket peer incarnation, pinned run-file identities, and exact launchd registration when present. Revalidate under the reservation before mutation.\n  - Response: Refuse cutover and leave the existing service and files intact. Surface the reason through the ordinary update result.\n  - User impact: Existing service remains available when it has not been stopped.\n- **Legacy daemon fails to exit** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The exit observer times out or sees a replacement rather than verified exit of the pinned incarnation.\n  - Response: Do not start a candidate. Preserve live or foreign publications. Reconcile only if ownership and exit can later be established.\n  - User impact: Update reports an actionable failure.\n- **Candidate registration, readiness, or publication fails** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: Exact job or supervisor identity does not match, child never reaches authenticated readiness, or outcome persistence fails.\n  - Response: Use journaled recovery to stop only the candidate generation, remove its exact job, restore the old selector and release, and restore prior running state. Keep the reservation fenced if rollback cannot be verified.\n  - User impact: A verified rollback reports failure and restores prior service.\n- **Legacy updater starts shutdown before staging the migration release** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The caller or installed release lacks the migration-capable preflight route.\n  - Response: Ship the migration preflight in the normal installer and updated clients. Test the exact older shipped entry points and provide the supported upgrade entry point when an old caller cannot carry migration. Never report migration success from the legacy acknowledgement.\n  - User impact: The user can use the ordinary supported install or update operation without launchd administration.\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Fresh installation with --no-start | Install the managed lifecycle with no daemon child. The first ordinary start uses the supervisor. |\n| Existing installation was stopped or is already managed | Preserve stopped state unless start was requested. Already managed updates use the normal managed transaction. |\n| Legacy shutdown exits early after broker denial | Require independent exact exit and reconcile only pinned run files before admitting a successor. Record the early exit distinctly from a successful drain. |\n| Concurrent installer, update, restart or retry | Single reservation owns cutover. A duplicate or interrupted operation reconciles its existing transaction before a new one starts. |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- Only one verified daemon owns the state root, PID file and socket. [[c2]]\n- Rollback preserves user settings, repositories, release and prior running state. [[c3]]\n- Linux retains its existing lifecycle. [[c1]]\n\n## 6. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `Node.js test runner through tsx, shell installer integration fixtures, and real macOS launchd smoke tests in a disposable user state root.`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — Check predecessor admission, persisted pins and recovery decisions.\n  - Subjects: `Fresh, managed, stopped legacy, direct legacy and passive LaunchAgent classifications`, `Refusal for foreign job, mismatched socket, changed descriptor and concurrent owners`, `Compatibility and backward decoding of existing journals`\n- **integration** — Exercise user entry points and verified cutover with isolated roots.\n  - Subjects: `Installer startup and --no-start`, `Release staging before legacy shutdown`, `Update from shipped broker-dependent predecessor through the normal supported entry point`, `Interrupted bootstrap, candidate failure, exact exit, rollback and retry`, `Linux installer and lifecycle regression`\n- **smoke** — Verify actual launchd registrations and processes in the macOS GUI domain.\n  - Subjects: `Fresh installer followed by ordinary restart and verified PID change`, `Existing direct and LaunchAgent installs with the broker returning errno 1`, `Recovery LaunchAgent descriptor and runtime flags`, `Restored running or stopped state and unchanged settings and data after failure`\n  - Fixtures: `Disposable macOS home with unique labels and isolated state`, `Pinned legacy and candidate builds`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `Fresh installer followed by ordinary restart and verified PID change`, `Installer startup and --no-start` |\n| `ac2` | `Update from shipped broker-dependent predecessor through the normal supported entry point`, `Existing direct and LaunchAgent installs with the broker returning errno 1`, `Recovery LaunchAgent descriptor and runtime flags` |\n| `ac3` | `Interrupted bootstrap, candidate failure, exact exit, rollback and retry`, `Restored running or stopped state and unchanged settings and data after failure`, `Linux installer and lifecycle regression` |\n\n## 7. Migration\n\n**State before:** The standard installer starts directly via daemon-ctl. The selector-gated supervisor and explicit LaunchAgent migration controller exist. See the installer and migration discovery bundle in s1.\n\n**State after:** Ordinary install and supported update commands establish a verified managed installation and use the per-user supervisor for future lifecycle calls.\n\n**Zero downtime:** no — **Data rewrite:** no\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Stage a compatible candidate and capture the canonical predecessor release and ownership before changing any live job or installation selector. — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Acquire the installation reservation and verify the supported predecessor shape. Record running state and exact job, runtime, and publication identities. — ↩ rollbackable\n3. For a running predecessor, request cooperative shutdown and verify exact exit. If an owned passive LaunchAgent exists, remove only its pinned registration after exit. Reconcile only owned files. — ↩ rollbackable\n4. Register the candidate supervisor and start one candidate only when the operation requests it or the predecessor was running. Verify service readiness, then publish the terminal outcome and release the reservation. — ↩ rollbackable\n5. On failure, resume the journal to restore the prior release, launch job and running or stopped state. Report any unresolved ownership with the installation fenced. — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** Keep existing installer switches, lifecycle command and IPC payload shapes. Keep Linux behavior. For the first upgrade, use a migration-capable normal installer or updated client before invoking older restart or shutdown behavior. A legacy binary that cannot stage the migration cannot promise automatic cutover. Decode existing managed and legacy-job journals.\n\n## 8. Alternatives considered\n\n### 8.1 a1: Integrate with existing lifecycle transactions — **CHOSEN**\n\nInstall or migrate through the existing entry points and shared state.\n\nFresh installation establishes the managed selector through an owned transaction. Existing updates resolve and pin the predecessor before using the shared update reservation and rollback.\n\n### 8.2 a2: Migrate at the next start\n\nDefer cutover until an ordinary start observes a stopped installation.\n\nAn update stages the release and start performs cutover after verifying that the legacy daemon has exited and no legacy job can relaunch it.\n\n**Rejected because:** Works for quiescent installs but fails the live automatic migration goal.\n\n## 9. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh`\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts`\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts`\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts`\n- **[[c5]]** `code` `src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts`\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `scripts/daemon-ctl.sh`\n- **[[c7]]** `code` `src/daemon/update-runner.ts`\n- **[[c8]]** `code` `src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts`\n- **[[c9]]** `prior-artifact` `ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f`\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-11T16:09:47.895Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition","title":"sequenceDefinition","kind":"visual"},{"id":"/body/companions","selector":"/body/companions","title":"companions","kind":"visual"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","title":"user","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","title":"controller","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","title":"legacy","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","title":"supervisor","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","selector":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","title":"daemon","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/5","selector":"/citations/5","title":"Citation 6","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/6","selector":"/citations/6","title":"Citation 7","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/7","selector":"/citations/7","title":"Citation 8","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/8","selector":"/citations/8","title":"Citation 9","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:25","selector":"document:line:25","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"},{"id":"document:line:89","selector":"document:line:89","title":"4. Diagrams","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"install","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The design follows the originating ISSUE's intent, but does not define executable entry-point routing, release provisioning, or fresh activation contracts sufficiently to resolve the demonstrated installer and updater gaps.","findings":[{"id":"install-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"LLD.md:109-112,167; /body/errorPaths","message":"The first-upgrade route remains unspecified. Requiring a migration-capable installer or updated client before shutdown does not identify how ordinary supported update commands obtain and invoke that code. The installed shell restart stops before fetching, and daemon.update schedules shutdown immediately after launching its installed helper. Current IDE lifecycle commands invoke the installed shell, while freshness flows use daemon.update. Define the supported command/client matrix, how each obtains the migration controller before shutdown, and the precise fallback for older callers. Otherwise the existing installation in the ISSUE can still enter the broker-dependent shutdown path before migration is available.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md: Fix intent","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:315-335","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:164-175,279-283","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:108-118","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts:108-118","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleCommandRunner.kt:38-50","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt:1393"]},{"id":"install-02","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:51,73,161; /body/contractDetails","message":"Immutable release staging and compatibility qualification are stated as preconditions without a provisioning contract. The installer currently fast-forwards and rebuilds the existing checkout in place. The migration controller instead requires separate prior/candidate roots, a candidate descriptor, and an explicit qualified release pair; the design does not assign production of those inputs, define their trusted source, or explain how a legacy release without a declaration is identified and qualified. Specify release layout, predecessor preservation before checkout/dependency mutation, qualification provenance, and refusal behavior. Without this, normal installation cannot satisfy the migration preconditions or guarantee an executable rollback release.","evidenceReferences":["scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:164-224","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:64-76","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts:102-109","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:109-123","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts:49-59","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md: Root cause"]},{"id":"install-03","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:34-54; /body/contractDetails/api/0","message":"The fresh activation contract cannot express its promised behavior. Its unchanged signature receives installation metadata, revalidation, and a legacy flag, but no requested-start state or activation reservation/journal. ManagedInstallation.enabled selects managed routing; it cannot also distinguish normal install from --no-start, since both must enable managed lifecycle. The existing function rejects enabled installations and only writes two exclusive-create files. Define the activation owner, explicit start intent, durable activation steps, and recovery from partial selector creation or bootstrap before claiming registration, conditional child startup, and interrupted activation as postconditions.","evidenceReferences":["src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts:22-30,284-300","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:41-54","src/cli/services/managed-daemon-control.ts:158-168,263-278","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:391-399","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:118"]},{"id":"install-04","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:119,167; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases","message":"The assertion that already managed updates use the normal managed transaction omits an existing blocking integration boundary. Shell update sends daemon.update, but the admin handler explicitly rejects that operation for managed daemons. A stopped managed installation also cannot service that RPC. Define how running and stopped managed update entry points invoke candidate preparation and the managed transaction, including the admin-handler change and regression coverage. Otherwise enabling management makes the ordinary update command unavailable.","evidenceReferences":["src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:126-128","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:325-328","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:108-111","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:127-136","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:135-149"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/contractDetails","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/daemon/update-runner.ts","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:95-119","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:109-165","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:274-336","src/cli/services/managed-daemon-control.ts:158-188,263-278","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleCommandRunner.kt:38-83","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:353-497","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-daemon-lifecycle.test.ts: test inventory","src/daemon/__tests__/update-handlers.test.ts: test inventory","src/config/__tests__/installer-defs.test.ts: test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The proposed unit, integration, and real macOS smoke levels are appropriate. Make the entry-point tests name the exact shipped predecessor/client combinations and include a second update after successful managed activation.","The acceptance mapping uses ac1–ac3 identifiers absent from the originating ISSUE. Label the corresponding fix-intent requirements explicitly so the mapping remains understandable."]},{"chunkId":"cutover","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The migration intent matches the ISSUE, but the LLD leaves predecessor-specific recovery contracts incomplete, does not fence legacy callers, and contradicts the existing durable commit rule.","findings":[{"id":"cutover-01","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:56-81; /body/contractDetails/api/1; /body/dataModelChanges","message":"The proposed discriminated predecessor record is described without defining its variants, persisted fields, decoding rules, or dispatch into migration and rollback. This is a material integration gap: completeLegacyMigration currently requires a saved LaunchAgent, recovery treats every predecessor without legacy metadata as managed, and journal validation requires such a prior pin to be enabled. A direct or stopped unmanaged predecessor therefore cannot enter the promised transaction safely. Define the variant contracts and backward decoding, including exact incarnation/publication evidence, direct-launch argv/environment/working directory, selector absence or baseline, and restoration verification. Also specify how recovery-job runtime flags are admitted: current legacy verification accepts only runtime plus entry, so additional Node flags are rejected despite the stated recovery-job coverage.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md:15","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: UpdatePredecessor and validPredecessor","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:137-218,274-302","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:57-93","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts:15-19,59-63","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts: verifyLegacyService","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:143"]},{"id":"cutover-02","severity":"HIGH","location":"LLD.md:121,161-165; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases; /body/migration","message":"A single installation reservation does not serialize legacy callers that never consult it. The design promises automatic live migration and concurrency safety but omits how older launchers, updaters and automatic starts are excluded during cutover. An already-running legacy shell/helper can rebuild the prior checkout or launch a daemon after predecessor exit while this transaction assumes exclusive ownership. The upstream lifecycle design explicitly requires legacy tooling that cannot honor the gate to be disabled for a quiescent cutover. Define an enforceable admission/exclusion boundary for supported live predecessors, including in-flight older callers, and refuse migration when that boundary cannot be established. Revalidation of the new journal alone cannot provide this guarantee.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: migration step 1","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh: prepare_daemon, start_prepared_daemon, cmd_restart and cmd_update","src/daemon/update-runner.ts: launchUpdate and runDetachedUpdate","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: reserve and admit","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts:77-92"]},{"id":"cutover-03","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:105-108,165-166; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/2; /body/migration","message":"Outcome-persistence failure is grouped with candidate registration/readiness failures and instructs recovery to stop the candidate and restore the predecessor. That is unsafe when publication throws after a durable success record was written. The existing transaction deliberately preserves the reservation on publication errors and classifies the durable outcome before selecting rollback or activation; committed success must never trigger implicit rollback. Define this distinction explicitly. Also distinguish provisional selector publication before supervisor bootstrap from terminal publication after readiness, since the current candidate handoff requires the former.","evidenceReferences":["src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: finish, settleManagedUpdate and recoverManagedTransaction","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: classifyMutationRecovery and publishOutcome","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts: stageManagedCandidate","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:46-76","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: migration steps 3-4"]},{"id":"cutover-04","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:75,120; /body/contractDetails/api/1; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases","message":"The LLD requires watchdog-denied early exit to be recorded distinctly from a successful drain, but supplies no evidence or result contract that can make that distinction. The cited cutover routine sends shutdown without reading its response and returns only the process incarnation after a boolean exact-exit observation. Its journal receipt records only exited plus that incarnation. Both clean drain and watchdog-arm failure therefore produce the same migration evidence. Specify a trustworthy classification source, persistence and user-visible result, with an explicit unknown classification when drain completion cannot be established. Add paired clean-drain and broker-denied predecessor tests; the existing synthetic exit fixture proves identity and cleanup only.","evidenceReferences":["src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts:29-31,79-93","src/shared/darwin-lifecycle.ts: DarwinExitObservation and observeDarwinExit","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:287-295","src/daemon/shutdown.ts: failClosed and begin","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts:13-57","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: legacy or temporary recovery instance edge case"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json: reproduction, rootCause and fixIntent","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: contracts, data model, error paths, tests and migration","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts","src/shared/darwin-lifecycle.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/update-runner.ts","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:210-345","src/daemon/shutdown.ts:155-210","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:350-497","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts: test inventory and publication-failure test","src/shared/__tests__/installation-mutation-gate.test.ts: test inventory","src/shared/__tests__/darwin-lifecycle.test.ts: test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Expand the proposed interruption tests into a predecessor-by-boundary matrix: before and after shutdown, exact-exit receipt, job removal, provisional selector writes, candidate registration, child readiness, terminal publication and reservation release. Include changed publications, timeouts, legacy callers racing cutover, and backward journal decoding.","Keep stopped-state validation explicit: successful migration should verify an authenticated idle supervisor and absent daemon publications without requiring daemon readiness."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"All assigned source units and the generated companion were inspected. The sequence omits substantive stopped-state and rollback paths. Actual rendering could not be verified because the browser host was unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/messages/5–8; sequence-diagram.html","message":"The generated sequence proceeds from conditional child startup to unconditional daemon readiness, so it does not represent successful --no-start or previously stopped completion. Rollback exists only in a message description that the generated diagram omits; no failure/restoration path is visible. Add explicit running/stopped and failure branches showing verified stopped completion, candidate cleanup, predecessor restoration, and fenced recovery when restoration cannot be verified. These are substantive lifecycle outcomes promised by the ISSUE and LLD.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded sequenceDiagram","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:54,105–108,118–119,164–165","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md: Fix intent","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: requireReady","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: settleManagedUpdate"]},{"id":"visuals-02","severity":"LOW","location":"LLD.md:91","message":"The companion hyperlink repeats the repository-relative document directory. Resolved relative to LLD.md, its target does not exist, although the canonical companion path does exist. Use a document-relative sequence-diagram.html link or an explicitly supported repository-root link.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:91",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/companions/0/relPath"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/companions","document:line:89","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/cli/services/managed-daemon-control.ts: openManagedSupervisorLink","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: completeLegacyMigration, requireReady, Rollback","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts"],"limitations":["Actual rendering of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html was not verified: the browser tool reported that its access host was unavailable. Embedded Mermaid source was inspected, but visual layout, clipping, and runtime rendering remain unverified."],"advice":["Clarify actor responsibilities in the sequence: exact-exit verification and passive-job removal are controller operations, whereas the current legacy-to-controller message labels them as a predecessor response. Separating launchd from the legacy daemon would make registration and removal ownership clearer.","A corrected sequence plus the existing ownership/cardinality prose should suffice; no additional ERD or UX artifact is necessary for this assignment."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Whole-artifact consistency checks found no additional defects beyond the accepted install, cutover, and visuals findings. The LLD covers the originating ISSUE's intended scope, but the recorded contract and integration gaps remain unresolved. Live and canonical documents match the review baseline. Mandatory visual verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid and viewer source","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: ownership, admission, compatibility, recovery, tests and migration contracts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts: installation types and input contracts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:274-345","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:145-190","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:100-122","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:145-230","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:350-415"],"limitations":["Mandatory actual rendering verification of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains outstanding. The completed visuals feedback records an unavailable browser access host; this consistency check inspected generated source and its agreement with the canonical definition, but did not establish runtime rendering, layout or clipping."],"advice":["Retain install-01 through install-04: together they cover first-upgrade delivery, immutable release provisioning, fresh activation intent and recovery, and running/stopped managed update routing. These are dependencies of the ordinary install/update promise, rather than separate optional enhancements.","Retain cutover-01 through cutover-04: predecessor variants and recovery-job flags, exclusion of legacy writers, durable commit classification, and trustworthy drain-versus-early-exit evidence must agree across the controller, journal, recovery implementation and tests.","Retain visuals-01 and visuals-02. Align the sequence's stopped completion and rollback branches with the eventual contracts, and correct its document-relative link.","Give ac1–ac3 explicit originating-ISSUE requirement labels. The ISSUE has no such identifiers; its fix intent nevertheless supplies the requirements for fresh start/restart, automatic supported migration, recovery jobs, direct installs, broker-denied exit, rollback preservation and Linux behavior.","Implementation tests and real macOS lifecycle smoke execution were not run during this read-only design review; their execution belongs to subsequent implementation qualification."]}],"progress":{"status":"incomplete","phase":"complete","completedChunks":4,"totalChunks":4,"lastMeaningfulActivityAt":null,"activeToolCount":0,"requiresUserInput":false,"checkpointPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json","sequence":0,"reviewElapsedMs":0,"unitElapsedMs":null,"observedAt":"2026-11-11T16:17:16.156Z","freshness":"stored"},"startedAt":"2026-11-11T16:09:47.897Z","reviewer":"daemon","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","unit":{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","executionId":"134af56d-02a3-4c10-bf8b-1bf476482494","dispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[]},"plan":{"chunks":[{"id":"install","title":"Installer activation and supported update entry points","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/contractDetails","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/8"],"concerns":["Trace fresh installation and automatic existing-install migration to the originating ISSUE reproduction, root cause and fix intent; use issue ancestry rather than inferred HLD ancestry.","Inspect installer, lifecycle controller, shell routing and update-runner evidence for concrete migration-capable entry points, candidate staging before legacy shutdown, compatibility qualification and immutable release availability.","Assess stageManagedInstallation inputs, activation ownership, launchd registration, GUI-domain preconditions, requested-start semantics, --no-start, interrupted activation and user-visible failures.","Check preserved installer switches, lifecycle commands and IPC payloads, current IDE client integration where necessary, Linux behavior and explicit scope boundaries.","Assess relevant unit, integration and macOS smoke coverage, acceptance traceability, alternatives and unresolved decisions."],"dependsOn":[],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"cutover","title":"Predecessor ownership, migration transaction and rollback","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8"],"concerns":["Inspect completeLegacyMigration and shared installation, update, legacy-job and cutover code for implementable ownership contracts and transaction boundaries.","Assess predecessor discrimination for managed, direct, passive LaunchAgent, temporary recovery-job and stopped installations; verify runtime, entry, socket peer incarnation, run-file identities and rollback launch metadata.","Check state-root, selector, supervisor, child and reservation ownership/cardinality, durable pins, journal compatibility and recovery fencing.","Trace exact Darwin exit observation through broker denial, early shutdown, timeout and replacement races; assess when pinned jobs and publications may safely be removed.","Assess candidate registration, readiness, publication, durable outcome ordering, interruption recovery and rollback preserving prior release, running state, settings and repository data.","Check concurrency, retries, failure reporting and test coverage for each supported predecessor and transaction failure boundary."],"dependsOn":["install"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"visuals","title":"Lifecycle sequence definitions and generated companion","selectors":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/companions","document:line:89"],"concerns":["Read the authored sequence, participant descriptions and linked generated HTML; inspect actual rendering where available and explicitly report unavailable mandatory visual verification as a limitation.","Check participant responsibilities and message direction against actual installer, controller, launchd, supervisor and daemon ownership.","Assess whether the sequence adequately represents staging, reservation, predecessor exit, registration, conditional start, readiness, stopped-state completion and rollback.","Verify companion paths, generated content and agreement with the source definition and substantive lifecycle contracts; assess whether further relationship or interaction artifacts are necessary."],"dependsOn":["install","cutover"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Whole-artifact requirements and shared-contract consistency","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all substantive assessments against the actual originating ISSUE, including fresh start/restart, automatic supported updates, recovery jobs, direct installs, broker-denied exit, rollback preservation and Linux behavior.","Check missing requirements, contradictions, shared signatures and state contracts, dependency/order feasibility, acceptance mappings, citations and canonical/live/generated-document agreement.","Ensure limitations distinguish missing mandatory inspection from optional execution, findings identify demonstrated defects with evidence, and final status follows the required precedence."],"dependsOn":["install","cutover","visuals"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 31 inventory units map to substantive chunks. Shared contracts, error paths and tests are assigned to both entry-point activation and migration recovery so each responsibility retains its interfaces, logic, failures and validation. Visual units receive separate source and rendering inspection after their lifecycle dependencies. The final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk and does not substitute for unit coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"document:line:25","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"document:line:89","chunkIds":["visuals"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"install","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"cutover","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"visuals","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":2,"MED":7,"LOW":1},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"install","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The design follows the originating ISSUE's intent, but does not define executable entry-point routing, release provisioning, or fresh activation contracts sufficiently to resolve the demonstrated installer and updater gaps.","findings":[{"id":"install-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"LLD.md:109-112,167; /body/errorPaths","message":"The first-upgrade route remains unspecified. Requiring a migration-capable installer or updated client before shutdown does not identify how ordinary supported update commands obtain and invoke that code. The installed shell restart stops before fetching, and daemon.update schedules shutdown immediately after launching its installed helper. Current IDE lifecycle commands invoke the installed shell, while freshness flows use daemon.update. Define the supported command/client matrix, how each obtains the migration controller before shutdown, and the precise fallback for older callers. Otherwise the existing installation in the ISSUE can still enter the broker-dependent shutdown path before migration is available.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md: Fix intent","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:315-335","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:164-175,279-283","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:108-118","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts:108-118","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleCommandRunner.kt:38-50","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt:1393"]},{"id":"install-02","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:51,73,161; /body/contractDetails","message":"Immutable release staging and compatibility qualification are stated as preconditions without a provisioning contract. The installer currently fast-forwards and rebuilds the existing checkout in place. The migration controller instead requires separate prior/candidate roots, a candidate descriptor, and an explicit qualified release pair; the design does not assign production of those inputs, define their trusted source, or explain how a legacy release without a declaration is identified and qualified. Specify release layout, predecessor preservation before checkout/dependency mutation, qualification provenance, and refusal behavior. Without this, normal installation cannot satisfy the migration preconditions or guarantee an executable rollback release.","evidenceReferences":["scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:164-224","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:64-76","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts:102-109","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:109-123","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts:49-59","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md: Root cause"]},{"id":"install-03","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:34-54; /body/contractDetails/api/0","message":"The fresh activation contract cannot express its promised behavior. Its unchanged signature receives installation metadata, revalidation, and a legacy flag, but no requested-start state or activation reservation/journal. ManagedInstallation.enabled selects managed routing; it cannot also distinguish normal install from --no-start, since both must enable managed lifecycle. The existing function rejects enabled installations and only writes two exclusive-create files. Define the activation owner, explicit start intent, durable activation steps, and recovery from partial selector creation or bootstrap before claiming registration, conditional child startup, and interrupted activation as postconditions.","evidenceReferences":["src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts:22-30,284-300","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:41-54","src/cli/services/managed-daemon-control.ts:158-168,263-278","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:391-399","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:118"]},{"id":"install-04","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:119,167; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases","message":"The assertion that already managed updates use the normal managed transaction omits an existing blocking integration boundary. Shell update sends daemon.update, but the admin handler explicitly rejects that operation for managed daemons. A stopped managed installation also cannot service that RPC. Define how running and stopped managed update entry points invoke candidate preparation and the managed transaction, including the admin-handler change and regression coverage. Otherwise enabling management makes the ordinary update command unavailable.","evidenceReferences":["src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:126-128","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:325-328","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:108-111","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:127-136","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:135-149"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/contractDetails","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/daemon/update-runner.ts","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:95-119","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:109-165","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:274-336","src/cli/services/managed-daemon-control.ts:158-188,263-278","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleCommandRunner.kt:38-83","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:353-497","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-daemon-lifecycle.test.ts: test inventory","src/daemon/__tests__/update-handlers.test.ts: test inventory","src/config/__tests__/installer-defs.test.ts: test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The proposed unit, integration, and real macOS smoke levels are appropriate. Make the entry-point tests name the exact shipped predecessor/client combinations and include a second update after successful managed activation.","The acceptance mapping uses ac1–ac3 identifiers absent from the originating ISSUE. Label the corresponding fix-intent requirements explicitly so the mapping remains understandable."]},{"chunkId":"cutover","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The migration intent matches the ISSUE, but the LLD leaves predecessor-specific recovery contracts incomplete, does not fence legacy callers, and contradicts the existing durable commit rule.","findings":[{"id":"cutover-01","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:56-81; /body/contractDetails/api/1; /body/dataModelChanges","message":"The proposed discriminated predecessor record is described without defining its variants, persisted fields, decoding rules, or dispatch into migration and rollback. This is a material integration gap: completeLegacyMigration currently requires a saved LaunchAgent, recovery treats every predecessor without legacy metadata as managed, and journal validation requires such a prior pin to be enabled. A direct or stopped unmanaged predecessor therefore cannot enter the promised transaction safely. Define the variant contracts and backward decoding, including exact incarnation/publication evidence, direct-launch argv/environment/working directory, selector absence or baseline, and restoration verification. Also specify how recovery-job runtime flags are admitted: current legacy verification accepts only runtime plus entry, so additional Node flags are rejected despite the stated recovery-job coverage.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md:15","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: UpdatePredecessor and validPredecessor","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:137-218,274-302","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:57-93","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts:15-19,59-63","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts: verifyLegacyService","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:143"]},{"id":"cutover-02","severity":"HIGH","location":"LLD.md:121,161-165; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases; /body/migration","message":"A single installation reservation does not serialize legacy callers that never consult it. The design promises automatic live migration and concurrency safety but omits how older launchers, updaters and automatic starts are excluded during cutover. An already-running legacy shell/helper can rebuild the prior checkout or launch a daemon after predecessor exit while this transaction assumes exclusive ownership. The upstream lifecycle design explicitly requires legacy tooling that cannot honor the gate to be disabled for a quiescent cutover. Define an enforceable admission/exclusion boundary for supported live predecessors, including in-flight older callers, and refuse migration when that boundary cannot be established. Revalidation of the new journal alone cannot provide this guarantee.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: migration step 1","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh: prepare_daemon, start_prepared_daemon, cmd_restart and cmd_update","src/daemon/update-runner.ts: launchUpdate and runDetachedUpdate","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: reserve and admit","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts:77-92"]},{"id":"cutover-03","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:105-108,165-166; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/2; /body/migration","message":"Outcome-persistence failure is grouped with candidate registration/readiness failures and instructs recovery to stop the candidate and restore the predecessor. That is unsafe when publication throws after a durable success record was written. The existing transaction deliberately preserves the reservation on publication errors and classifies the durable outcome before selecting rollback or activation; committed success must never trigger implicit rollback. Define this distinction explicitly. Also distinguish provisional selector publication before supervisor bootstrap from terminal publication after readiness, since the current candidate handoff requires the former.","evidenceReferences":["src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: finish, settleManagedUpdate and recoverManagedTransaction","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: classifyMutationRecovery and publishOutcome","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts: stageManagedCandidate","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:46-76","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: migration steps 3-4"]},{"id":"cutover-04","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:75,120; /body/contractDetails/api/1; /body/errorPaths/edgeCases","message":"The LLD requires watchdog-denied early exit to be recorded distinctly from a successful drain, but supplies no evidence or result contract that can make that distinction. The cited cutover routine sends shutdown without reading its response and returns only the process incarnation after a boolean exact-exit observation. Its journal receipt records only exited plus that incarnation. Both clean drain and watchdog-arm failure therefore produce the same migration evidence. Specify a trustworthy classification source, persistence and user-visible result, with an explicit unknown classification when drain completion cannot be established. Add paired clean-drain and broker-denied predecessor tests; the existing synthetic exit fixture proves identity and cleanup only.","evidenceReferences":["src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts:29-31,79-93","src/shared/darwin-lifecycle.ts: DarwinExitObservation and observeDarwinExit","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:287-295","src/daemon/shutdown.ts: failClosed and begin","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts:13-57","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: legacy or temporary recovery instance edge case"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json: reproduction, rootCause and fixIntent","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: contracts, data model, error paths, tests and migration","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts","src/shared/darwin-lifecycle.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/update-runner.ts","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:210-345","src/daemon/shutdown.ts:155-210","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:350-497","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts: test inventory and publication-failure test","src/shared/__tests__/installation-mutation-gate.test.ts: test inventory","src/shared/__tests__/darwin-lifecycle.test.ts: test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Expand the proposed interruption tests into a predecessor-by-boundary matrix: before and after shutdown, exact-exit receipt, job removal, provisional selector writes, candidate registration, child readiness, terminal publication and reservation release. Include changed publications, timeouts, legacy callers racing cutover, and backward journal decoding.","Keep stopped-state validation explicit: successful migration should verify an authenticated idle supervisor and absent daemon publications without requiring daemon readiness."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"All assigned source units and the generated companion were inspected. The sequence omits substantive stopped-state and rollback paths. Actual rendering could not be verified because the browser host was unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/messages/5–8; sequence-diagram.html","message":"The generated sequence proceeds from conditional child startup to unconditional daemon readiness, so it does not represent successful --no-start or previously stopped completion. Rollback exists only in a message description that the generated diagram omits; no failure/restoration path is visible. Add explicit running/stopped and failure branches showing verified stopped completion, candidate cleanup, predecessor restoration, and fenced recovery when restoration cannot be verified. These are substantive lifecycle outcomes promised by the ISSUE and LLD.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded sequenceDiagram","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:54,105–108,118–119,164–165","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md: Fix intent","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: requireReady","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: settleManagedUpdate"]},{"id":"visuals-02","severity":"LOW","location":"LLD.md:91","message":"The companion hyperlink repeats the repository-relative document directory. Resolved relative to LLD.md, its target does not exist, although the canonical companion path does exist. Use a document-relative sequence-diagram.html link or an explicitly supported repository-root link.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:91",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/companions/0/relPath"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/companions","document:line:89","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/cli/services/managed-daemon-control.ts: openManagedSupervisorLink","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: completeLegacyMigration, requireReady, Rollback","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts"],"limitations":["Actual rendering of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html was not verified: the browser tool reported that its access host was unavailable. Embedded Mermaid source was inspected, but visual layout, clipping, and runtime rendering remain unverified."],"advice":["Clarify actor responsibilities in the sequence: exact-exit verification and passive-job removal are controller operations, whereas the current legacy-to-controller message labels them as a predecessor response. Separating launchd from the legacy daemon would make registration and removal ownership clearer.","A corrected sequence plus the existing ownership/cardinality prose should suffice; no additional ERD or UX artifact is necessary for this assignment."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Whole-artifact consistency checks found no additional defects beyond the accepted install, cutover, and visuals findings. The LLD covers the originating ISSUE's intended scope, but the recorded contract and integration gaps remain unresolved. Live and canonical documents match the review baseline. Mandatory visual verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid and viewer source","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: ownership, admission, compatibility, recovery, tests and migration contracts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts: installation types and input contracts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:274-345","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:145-190","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:100-122","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:145-230","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:350-415"],"limitations":["Mandatory actual rendering verification of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains outstanding. The completed visuals feedback records an unavailable browser access host; this consistency check inspected generated source and its agreement with the canonical definition, but did not establish runtime rendering, layout or clipping."],"advice":["Retain install-01 through install-04: together they cover first-upgrade delivery, immutable release provisioning, fresh activation intent and recovery, and running/stopped managed update routing. These are dependencies of the ordinary install/update promise, rather than separate optional enhancements.","Retain cutover-01 through cutover-04: predecessor variants and recovery-job flags, exclusion of legacy writers, durable commit classification, and trustworthy drain-versus-early-exit evidence must agree across the controller, journal, recovery implementation and tests.","Retain visuals-01 and visuals-02. Align the sequence's stopped completion and rollback branches with the eventual contracts, and correct its document-relative link.","Give ac1–ac3 explicit originating-ISSUE requirement labels. The ISSUE has no such identifiers; its fix intent nevertheless supplies the requirements for fresh start/restart, automatic supported migration, recovery jobs, direct installs, broker-denied exit, rollback preservation and Linux behavior.","Implementation tests and real macOS lifecycle smoke execution were not run during this read-only design review; their execution belongs to subsequent implementation qualification."]}],"limitations":["Actual rendering of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html was not verified: the browser tool reported that its access host was unavailable. Embedded Mermaid source was inspected, but visual layout, clipping, and runtime rendering remain unverified.","Mandatory actual rendering verification of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains outstanding. The completed visuals feedback records an unavailable browser access host; this consistency check inspected generated source and its agreement with the canonical definition, but did not establish runtime rendering, layout or clipping."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"84b35629e7b712583748489d95b40e3d49d267770e5380579dedf1b3f21faa94"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-11T16:17:16.156Z"}]}}}}
